<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3794" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Artĕmĭta</span></b> , ae,
		or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Artĕmĭtē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρτέμιτα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city of Assyria</i> or, perh. more strictly, <i>of Babylonia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 26,
				30, § 117</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Another name for Rhene</i>, <i>one of
				the Echinades</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12, 22, §
		67</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
